============================================================
46. BREAK IN NESTED LOOPS
============================================================

Important:

break terminates only the nearest loop.

Example:

    for (int i = 0; i < 3; i++)
    {
        for (int j = 0; j < 3; j++)
        {
            if (j == 1)
                break;

            printf("%d %d\n", i, j);
        }
    }


The inner loop stops.

The outer loop continues.


============================================================
47. CONTINUE IN NESTED LOOPS
============================================================

continue affects the nearest loop in which it occurs.

Example:

    for (int i = 0; i < 3; i++)
    {
        for (int j = 0; j < 3; j++)
        {
            if (j == 1)
                continue;

            printf("%d %d\n", i, j);
        }
    }


Only j == 1 is skipped.


