    5 x 1 = 5
    5 x 2 = 10
    ...
    5 x 10 = 50


============================================================
81. PRACTICAL PROGRAM — FIBONACCI
============================================================

Generate first n Fibonacci numbers.

Example:

    0 1 1 2 3 5 8 ...


Program:

    int n = 10;
    unsigned long long a = 0;
    unsigned long long b = 1;

    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++)
    {
        printf("%llu ", a);

        unsigned long long next = a + b;
        a = b;
        b = next;
    }


Important:
Fixed-width integer overflow can occur for sufficiently
large n.


============================================================
82. PRACTICAL PROGRAM — GCD
============================================================

Euclidean algorithm:

    gcd(a, b)

repeatedly replaces:

    a, b

with:

    b, a % b


Example:

    int a = 48;
    int b = 18;

    while (b != 0)
    {
        int temp = b;
        b = a % b;
        a = temp;
    }

    printf("GCD = %d\n", a);


Output:

    GCD = 6


Complexity:

    O(log(min(a,b)))

for the standard Euclidean algorithm under usual assumptions.


