85. PRACTICAL PROGRAM — LINEAR SEARCH
============================================================

    int arr[] = {10, 20, 30, 40, 50};
    int n = sizeof(arr) / sizeof(arr[0]);
    int target = 30;
    int index = -1;

    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++)
    {
        if (arr[i] == target)
        {
            index = i;
            break;
        }
    }

    printf("Index = %d\n", index);


Time complexity:

    O(n)


